{"body": [{"author": {"avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/456674?v=4", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/events{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/BurntSushi", "id": 456674, "login": "BurntSushi", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjY3NA==", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi", "user_view_type": "public"}, "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits/2bcd2b41470706fac9e9e995be3721caf2271b02/comments", "commit": {"author": {"date": "2025-03-14T14:55:00Z", "email": "andrew@astral.sh", "name": "Andrew Gallant"}, "comment_count": 0, "committer": {"date": "2025-03-14T18:46:17Z", "email": "jamslam@gmail.com", "name": "Andrew Gallant"}, "message": "red_knot: plumb through `DiagnosticFormat` to the CLI\n\nThe CLI calls this `OutputFormat`, and so does the type where the CLI is\ndefined. But it's called `DiagnosticFormat` in `ruff_db` to be\nconsistent with `DisplayDiagnosticConfig`.\n\nRef https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/15697#issuecomment-2706477278", "tree": {"sha": "e82bc9ee61135a6dfdb53451cc81aa7dbb18e6bb", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/trees/e82bc9ee61135a6dfdb53451cc81aa7dbb18e6bb"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/commits/2bcd2b41470706fac9e9e995be3721caf2271b02", "verification": {"payload": null, "reason": "unsigned", "signature": null, "verified": false, "verified_at": null}}, "committer": {"avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/456674?v=4", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/events{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/BurntSushi", "id": 456674, "login": "BurntSushi", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjY3NA==", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/BurntSushi", "user_view_type": "public"}, "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/2bcd2b41470706fac9e9e995be3721caf2271b02", "node_id": "C_kwDOHy0BzdoAKDJiY2QyYjQxNDcwNzA2ZmFjOWU5ZTk5NWJlMzcyMWNhZjIyNzFiMDI", "parents": [{"html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/eb6871d2090ae441d3b3dd0aed69b0fbcf396cba", "sha": "eb6871d2090ae441d3b3dd0aed69b0fbcf396cba", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits/eb6871d2090ae441d3b3dd0aed69b0fbcf396cba"}], "sha": "2bcd2b41470706fac9e9e995be3721caf2271b02", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits/2bcd2b41470706fac9e9e995be3721caf2271b02"}, {"author": {"avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1203881?v=4", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/events{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/MichaReiser", "id": 1203881, "login": "MichaReiser", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDM4ODE=", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/MichaReiser", "user_view_type": "public"}, "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits/678b0c2d393733ec33574db94e21d3eb4bdf2396/comments", "commit": {"author": {"date": "2025-02-10T14:28:45Z", "email": "micha@reiser.io", "name": "Micha Reiser"}, "comment_count": 0, "committer": {"date": "2025-02-10T14:28:45Z", "email": "noreply@github.com", "name": "GitHub"}, "message": "[red-knot] Resolve `Options` to `Settings` (#16000)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR generalize the idea that we may want to emit diagnostics for \ninvalid or incompatible configuration values similar to how we already \ndo it for `rules`. \n\nThis PR introduces a new `Settings` struct that is similar to `Options`\nbut, unlike\n`Options`, are fields have their default values filled in and they use a\nrepresentation optimized for reads.\n\nThe diagnostics created during loading the `Settings` are stored on the\n`Project` so that we can emit them when calling `check`.\n\nThe motivation for this work is that it simplifies adding new settings.\nThat's also why I went ahead and added the `terminal.error-on-warning`\nsetting to demonstrate how new settings are added.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nExisting tests, new CLI test.", "tree": {"sha": "2c6391d116649523cafc17b8e079c0228ed13aa6", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/trees/2c6391d116649523cafc17b8e079c0228ed13aa6"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/commits/678b0c2d393733ec33574db94e21d3eb4bdf2396", "verification": {"payload": "tree 2c6391d116649523cafc17b8e079c0228ed13aa6\nparent 524cf6e5155066132da772b9f84e2e6695f241b8\nauthor Micha Reiser <micha@reiser.io> 1739197725 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1739197725 +0100\n\n[red-knot] Resolve `Options` to `Settings` (#16000)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR generalize the idea that we may want to emit diagnostics for \ninvalid or incompatible configuration values similar to how we already \ndo it for `rules`. \n\nThis PR introduces a new `Settings` struct that is similar to `Options`\nbut, unlike\n`Options`, are fields have their default values filled in and they use a\nrepresentation optimized for reads.\n\nThe diagnostics created during loading the `Settings` are stored on the\n`Project` so that we can emit them when calling `check`.\n\nThe motivation for this work is that it simplifies adding new settings.\nThat's also why I went ahead and added the `terminal.error-on-warning`\nsetting to demonstrate how new settings are added.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nExisting tests, new CLI test.", "reason": "valid", "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJnqg0dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA46UQAHNVX3/ku+YfTD7zSqYIsyvK\n8NaOXO7cAsgy/hYsEkQvflZLliLwiVUxNLYZivl+TxSgGlQIQfHkg0nhuVLEGOyh\nCAnJEwl+ATLhmUmBqDrdylep7h28REqkys02zTAp71J58EkF/3rsu8NiH0W46PkR\nslG4wewZJ2TKQCUBDcyRL/O0xxORS1caJtBSXiRk81MkbDSew/L4jkYKSK4F7+i2\nUig15m9avlme/vCSlJbOWcdRQyBZIDORBnOsught7pkO04SbxxxjyosJb2Bp2TvK\nDnUifboNRHfaGuw+geR4rZyCh/3rIu/Xm9r8wDFbcabGGFy75ptvJ1efuxILXjVo\no3/tOwW116efBYhM4ElMVsKRXY4tykVRPAu+aBBjVyV2g/+xDSNJRTfS/zNyhEBF\nRVg4UW6b1C+JjCqYiMum689sDj+STuxPzzoeRi6lCjkQ4XetoLkPMPKh/vuhIe1R\nJ5eiWhsxr3XgYEStBPFc5KqBLGwKd9bpBkMJRd511fVLb1WsZ50Tc/UAjyiUv51S\nIYp/TewusuW2YwAdx+ay/UNE5yBJ1g6JLee0bqwQ2ZG8K+u0eiNmOA652oaUjsA/\nWjWz9nxA6re4QlFlnELb43qMvAnW0qeFqn1FW7aMgz9ArPNSzI7duR0i9KfdqkxO\